# API Information


main: {
  kit: {
    info: {
      contact: {
        url: "https://web.dragonball-api.com/documentation"
      }
      description: "The Dragon Ball API provides comprehensive information about characters, transformations, power stats, planets, and locations from the Dragon Ball universe. It allows users to retrieve data through various endpoints for easy integration into applications or services."
      servers: [
        {
          description: "Production server"
          url: "https://dragonball-api.com/api"
        }
      ]
      title: "Dragon Ball API"
      version: "1.0.0"
      tagline: "Query characters, transformations, power stats, planets, and locations from the Dragon Ball universe"
      homepage: "https://dragonball-api.com/"
      docs_url: "https://web.dragonball-api.com/documentation"
      about_md: `The Dragon Ball API is a free, community-run REST API that serves data drawn from the Dragon Ball franchise — characters, their transformations, power statistics, planets, and notable locations. Documentation and an interactive explorer are available at [web.dragonball-api.com](https://web.dragonball-api.com/documentation).

What you get from the API:

- Character records (e.g. \`/api/characters\`) covering figures across the Dragon Ball series
- Planet records (e.g. \`/api/planets\`) describing locations in the universe
- Transformation data linked to characters, with power-related stats

The API is open and requires no authentication. Endpoints generally return JSON over HTTPS. CORS is reported as disabled on the main endpoints, so browser-based clients may need a proxy.`
      entity_desc: {
        character: "A Dragon Ball character with biographical and combat-related fields, served from `/api/characters`."
        planet: "A planet or notable location in the Dragon Ball universe, served from `/api/planets`."
        transformation: "A transformation belonging to a character, exposing the altered form and its associated power stats."
      }
      auth: false
    }
  }
}
